From 28bde7aa731a7b55c59c5cc325f724cd31bd4f43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "visy (bbport)" <noreply@bbport>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 18:54:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Launcher: an idle Nightwatch VPN tunnel disconnects and comes
 back when needed (visy 0.7.8 handoff)

A launcher left open held its tunnel forever (2026-10-31: 18 of 30 connected players were in no game), each one
an address and server capacity. Core/VpnIdle.cs (pure, SeamlessTests IdleRules) decides; the Co-op page acts
through the same ToggleVpn path as its button:
- disconnect after 10 min (vpn_idle_minutes) with the window in the background or minimized and no game running;
- reconnect when the window is activated, the Co-op tab is shown, or Play starts a host/join game (Play waits
  at most 15 s, then starts anyway);
- only for a connection the player made in this launcher and has not disconnected by hand; never while the
  game runs, during a connect/disconnect, or for another launcher's tunnel.
Setting: Co-op > Advanced networking "Disconnect the VPN when idle" (vpn_idle_disconnect, on by default).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
